  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Queries create the state they need only while holding back notifications during a change when they first change, and collection queries keep the caches of all but their four most common kinds of child query in one object created when the first such child is built, so every collection query is 256 B lighter: a source query fell from 816 B to 560 B, and building and disposing a seven-query chain over each of 256 one-element sources from 1,812 μs and 4,556 KB to 1,593 μs and 3,980 KB",
